Bugfix: Stop asking every auth module on each request of an existing session

A client that keeps its session cookie and sends a bearer token on every
request, such as the desktop and mobile clients with an OAuth2 token, had that
token checked by every installed auth module on each OCS and web request. With
the OpenID Connect app enabled this meant two requests to the identity provider
for each such request, an introspection call that could only fail and a
discovery fetch, because the OpenID Connect app cannot know that the token
belongs to the OAuth2 app. The session now remembers which auth module
established it. As long as that module confirms the session user, the other
apps' auth modules are no longer asked, while the built-in app password and
basic auth checks still have to agree. In every other case all modules are
asked as before.

